  "question": {
    "text": "The position vector of a moving body at any instant of time is given as $\\vec{r}=\\left(5 t^2 \\hat{i}-5 t \\hat{j}\\right) \\mathrm{m}$. The magnitude and direction of velocity at $t=2 \\mathrm{~s}$ is,",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5xO9b",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{15} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$, making an angle of $\\tan ^{-1} 4$ with - ve $Y$ axis",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9uCtD",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{15} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$, making an angle of $\\tan ^{-1} 4$ with + ve X axis",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7QV3f",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{17} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$, making an angle of $\\tan ^{-1} 4$ with + ve $X$ axis",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gSoCG",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{17} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$, making an angle of $\\tan ^{-1} 4$ with - ve $Y$ axis",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{r}}=5 t^2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-5 \\mathrm{t}_{\\mathrm{j}} \\\\ & \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}=10 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-5 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}} \\\\ & \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}=20 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-5 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}} \\quad \\text { at } \\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{sec}\\end{aligned}$\n\n\n\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ZOdpSkjDnDcpMwQYs-JT-1wiwxy8-x6KOSoVL11NtxU.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\tan \\theta=\\frac{20}{5}=4 \\\\ & \\theta=\\tan ^{-1} 4 \\\\ & \\text { From -veY-axis }\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
